## 6. What I take from this

The error in §1 is the kind Rule 1 of `_RULES_OF_ENGAGEMENT` is built to catch: the arithmetic in W01 was correct, the Gaussian integrals were right, and the whole thing was still measuring the wrong object. Reading it against itself would not have found that. Only checking it against the definition of \(P_r^{MS}\) — or re-running it under the correct weighting — would.

That is the same failure mode as `CL-ERR-013`, one level up: not an unstable number, but a stable number for a quantity nobody asked about.
